{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And you shall dash.</b> With a vessel — he holds the מִזְרָק and dashes against the horn so that it is visible on both sides. And no offering requires application by finger except a חַטָּאת alone, but other slaughter-offerings require neither horn nor finger, for their blood is applied from the middle of the altar and below, and he does not go up the ramp but stands on the ground and dashes (Zevachim 55)." "<b>All around.</b> Thus is explained in שְׁחִיטַת קָדָשִׁים that סָבִיב is nothing but two applications that are four: one on this corner-horn, and one opposite it on the diagonal corner. And each application is visible on both sides of the horn, this way and that — so the blood is placed in the four directions all around; therefore it is called סָבִיב."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:30.292766672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}